        "date": "2026-11-26T15:51:33Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): document component table and undoable assembly commands\n\nThe document holds shared tool components (DocumentComponents) and\neach tool its component stack (ToolAssembly). Four undoable commands:\nUpsertDocumentComponent, EditDocumentComponent (live update of every\ntool built from the component, in one undo step, refused whole by\nname), DeleteDocumentComponent (refuses a used component, names the\ntools) and SetToolAssembly (lands the derived ToolDef and ToolBody).\nOperations go Stale by their stamps. DeleteTool keeps the stack.\n\nFixes #3644\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
